Licence for the code
====================

"Code" means very different things on either side of this repository, and that
asymmetry is why the licences are split at all.

In combinatorial-optimization/, the code is part of the course: colib/, the
labs, their tests and the reference solutions are real software that a reader
studies, runs and writes against.

In mechanics-to-relativity/, the code is not part of the course: mrlib/ and
build/ are the machinery that produced the material. Nobody studies them.

Also covered: both courses' site builders (combinatorial-optimization/slides/
site/build.py and mechanics-to-relativity/mrlib/site_build.py), the authoring
and checking tools under each course's slides/tools/, and site/build_all.py.

The taught material of both courses is licensed separately; see
LICENSE-CONTENT.

